\subsection{Phase C: exact large-angle $\SO(3)$ measurement geometry}
\label{sec:stability-widening-phase-c}

The deployed nonlinear certificate is stated directly on the rotation group and
on source-reachable Kalman corrections.  No common-radius or componentwise
radius relaxation is used in the primary certificate chain.  Velocity,
position, integral displacement, latent acceleration, and accelerometer bias
remain in the exact source state and covariance recursion; their influence on
attitude is retained through the actual accepted innovations and Kalman gains.

Let
\begin{equation}
 \mat R_e:=\widehat{\mat R}\mat R^\top\in\SO(3),
 \qquad
 V_R(\mat R_e):=\frac12\operatorname{tr}(\mat I-\mat R_e)
 =1-\cos\theta_e,
 \label{eq:widen-SO3-energy}
\end{equation}
where $\theta_e\in[0,\pi]$ is the geodesic attitude error.  Define also
\begin{equation}
 \vct e_R:=\operatorname{vex}\!\left(
 \frac{\mat R_e-\mat R_e^\top}{2}\right)
 =\sin\theta_e\,\vct u_e.
 \label{eq:widen-SO3-gradient}
\end{equation}
For every fixed $0<\theta_*<\pi$ and
$0\le\theta_e\le\theta_*$,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1-\cos\theta_*}{\theta_*^2}\theta_e^2
 \le V_R(\mat R_e)\le\frac12\theta_e^2.
 \label{eq:widen-SO3-sector}
\end{equation}
Thus $V_R$ is an exact nonlocal chart energy.  It is not, however, assumed to
be a Lyapunov function for an anisotropic Kalman correction.

The implementation injects and resets after each accepted measurement.  Hence
one source correction event $g\in\{a,m,S\}$ has
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct d_{k,g}:=\Delta\vct\theta_{k,g}
 =\mat E_\theta\mat K_{g,k}\vct r_{g,k},
 \qquad \vct r_{S,k}=-\delta\vct S,}
 \label{eq:widen-exact-source-correction}
\end{equation}
with $\vct d_{k,g}=0$ on a rejected/not-due branch.  The next accepted gain is
formed from the covariance after the preceding Joseph update and left-error
reset; gains from different source times are never added as though they were
simultaneous.  Equation~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-source-correction} therefore
retains the full $S\to\theta$ cross-covariance path and all non-attitude terms
in the accelerometer correction without a block-diagonal or Schmidt-style
proof modification.

The source calls \texttt{quat\_from\_delta\_theta}.  Outside its small series
branch the injected rotation is exactly
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal R(q_c(\vct d))=\exp([\vct d]_\times),}
 \label{eq:widen-exact-injection}
\end{equation}
and the normalized series branch differs from that exponential by a sixth-order
geodesic defect:
\begin{equation}
 d_{\SO(3)}\!\left(
 \mathcal R(q_c(\vct d)),\exp([\vct d]_\times)\right)
 \le c_s\|\vct d\|^6,
 \qquad \|\vct d\|\le10^{-2}.
 \label{eq:widen-series-defect}
\end{equation}
The computer-assisted map evaluates the deployed series branch itself; the
bound above is retained only for analytic comparison with the ideal exponential.

For one ideal exponential correction the physical attitude error satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \mat R_e^+=\exp([\vct d_{k,g}]_\times)\mat R_e^-.
 \label{eq:widen-exact-attitude-update}
\end{equation}
Let $\delta=\|\vct d_{k,g}\|$ and define the continuous functions
$\operatorname{sinc}\delta:=\sin\delta/\delta$ and
$\operatorname{cosc}\delta:=(1-\cos\delta)/\delta^2$ with their limiting values
at zero.  Rodrigues' identity gives
\begin{align}
 V_R(\mat R_e^+)-V_R(\mat R_e^-)
 &=\operatorname{sinc}(\delta)\,
   \vct d_{k,g}^\top\vct e_R^-
 \nonumber\\
 &\quad-\frac12\operatorname{cosc}(\delta)
   \operatorname{tr}\!\left(
   [\vct d_{k,g}]_\times^2\mat R_e^-\right).
 \label{eq:widen-exact-energy-change}
\end{align}
Equation~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change} is exact for arbitrary finite
$\vct d_{k,g}$ and does not replace $\sin\theta_e$ by $\theta_e$ or bound the
finite correction by a generic quadratic Taylor remainder.

\begin{lemma}[Exact finite-correction group identity]
\label{lem:widen-exact-group-identity}
For every $\mat R_e\in\SO(3)$ and every finite correction $\vct d$, the update
of Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-attitude-update} satisfies
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change}.  Hence the change of the physical
trace energy can be evaluated exactly for the actual source gain; no sign is
assumed a priori.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Substitute Rodrigues' formula
$\exp([d]_\times)=I+\operatorname{sinc}(\delta)[d]_\times+
\operatorname{cosc}(\delta)[d]_\times^2$ into
$V_R(R^+)-V_R(R^-)=-\tfrac12\operatorname{tr}((\exp([d]_\times)-I)R^-)$.  The
identity
$\operatorname{tr}([d]_\times R)=-2d^\top
\operatorname{vex}((R-R^\top)/2)$ gives the first term and the second Rodrigues
term gives the remaining trace exactly.
\end{proof}

The implemented covariance reset is
\begin{equation}
 \mat G_r(\vct d)=\mat I+\frac12[\vct d]_\times,
 \label{eq:widen-reset-G}
\end{equation}
with
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\mat G_r(\vct d)\|_2
 =\sqrt{1+\frac14\|\vct d\|^2},
 \qquad
 \det\mat G_r=1+\frac14\|\vct d\|^2>0.}
 \label{eq:widen-reset-G-bound}
\end{equation}
Thus neither the state injection nor the covariance reset has a singularity at
an unwrapped correction norm of $\pi$.

\subsubsection{Why the raw $V_R$ sector is not the implementation certificate}

A single accepted vector measurement has an exact rotation-about-vector null
direction, so no positive full-attitude coefficient can hold for every
individual accelerometer or magnetometer correction.  More importantly, even a
noncollinear accelerometer--magnetometer packet need not decrease the isotropic
trace energy under an anisotropic Kalman gain.  The source-correlated verifier
\texttt{ou3\_p5\_large\_angle\_sector\_certificate.py} evaluates the actual
H-mode goLive covariance, recomputes the accepted gains sequentially with
validated interval Kalman arithmetic, applies the Joseph covariance update and
implemented left-error reset between them, and evaluates both the deployed
quaternion map and Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change}.  It certifies an
admissible zero-$\vct\xi$ witness strictly inside both gauged handoff nodes for
which
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr D_{R}:=V_R(\mat R_e^-)-V_R(\mat R_e^+)<0.
 \label{eq:widen-group-dissipation}
\end{equation}
Consequently no choice of finite $\beta_R$ can make
$\mathscr D_R\ge\alpha_RV_R-\beta_R\|\xi\|^2$ hold with
$\alpha_R>0$ on the declared complete source family: the witness has
$\xi=0$ and $V_R>0$.  Increasing $\beta_R$ would therefore be a theorem-gate
relaxation, not a certificate widening.

The exact group identity remains useful, but the quantitative Lyapunov energy
must follow the same source-shaped information geometry as P3--P4.  Let
\begin{equation}
 \vct z_i(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 :=\begin{bmatrix}\vct c(\mat R_e)\\\vct\xi\end{bmatrix},
 \qquad
 \vct c(\mat R_e)=2\tan(\theta_e/2)\vct u_e,
\end{equation}
and partition the positive node matrix of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-group-metric} as
\begin{equation}
 \overline{\mat P}_i=
 \begin{bmatrix}
  \mat A_i&\mat B_i\\
  \mat B_i^\top&\mat C_i
 \end{bmatrix},
 \qquad
 \mat Q_{R,i}:=\mat A_i-\mat B_i\mat C_i^{-1}\mat B_i^\top\succ0.
\end{equation}
Define the source-shaped attitude energy
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{I,i}(\mat R_e):=
 \vct c(\mat R_e)^\top\mat Q_{R,i}\vct c(\mat R_e).}
 \label{eq:widen-information-attitude-energy}
\end{equation}
This is a genuine group energy on every $\theta_{*,i}<\pi$ chart, but unlike
$V_R$ it retains the directional covariance/information geometry that generated
the Kalman gain.

Let $w:i\to j$ be one bounded source-correlated correction packet/word in the
same language used by P3--P4, including the required noncollinear vector event.
Let $\mathcal F_w$ be the exact ordered source map, including every intervening
prediction, accepted/rejected correction, Joseph update, quaternion injection,
and reset.  Individual corrections are required to remain prefix safe; strict
full-attitude decrease is a packet/word property, not a one-vector property.
Writing $R_w^+$ for the attitude component of $\mathcal F_w$, define
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr D_{I,w}(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 :=V_{I,i}(\mat R_e)-V_{I,j}(\mat R_w^+).
\end{equation}
The corrected large-angle sector required for P5 is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathscr D_{I,w}(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 \ge \alpha_{I,i}V_{I,i}(\mat R_e)
      -\beta_{I,i}\|\vct\xi\|^2,
 \qquad \alpha_{I,i}>0,\quad\beta_{I,i}<\infty.}
 \label{eq:widen-large-angle-sector}
\end{equation}
Every matrix, gain, source parameter, and branch in one evaluation belongs to
the same jointly source-reachable tuple.  Independent extrema are not multiplied
together.

\begin{theorem}[Metric-shaped large-angle source-word dissipation]
\label{thm:widen-large-angle-dissipation}
Suppose every source-complete full-heading outer word satisfies
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-sector} on a compact chart
$\theta_e\le\theta_{*,i}<\pi$, every exact source prefix remains in its declared
node, and the complete non-attitude part is bounded by the same node funnel.
Then the exact ordered word map admits a finite source-word Lyapunov decrease in
the Cayley/information metric.  The admissible attitude domain is set by the
verified group chart and source-word enclosure, not by a small-angle Taylor
radius.  Positive one-sample $V_R$ increments are allowed.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Complete the square in the node matrix to obtain
$W_i\ge V_{I,i}$ up to the fixed positive source scale.  Apply
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-sector} to the exact ordered packet and combine
its $\beta_{I,i}\|\xi\|^2$ term with the simultaneously enclosed additive-state
part of the same node metric.  Prefix safety keeps the Cayley coordinate and all
implemented quaternion/reset operations in the certified compact domain.  The
result is the source-word funnel inequality used in the P5 recursion.  No
per-correction monotonicity of the isotropic trace energy is invoked.
\end{proof}

\subsubsection{Exact effective vector inputs for the outer P5 word}
\label{sec:widen-effective-vector-input}

The complete outer-word enclosure can be sharpened further without changing the
filter.  The finite-angle vector residual need not be treated as an independent
measurement-space remainder when the shipping Jacobian either annihilates or
absorbs that residual exactly.

For the configured magnetometer, let $\vct v$ be the predicted body-frame field.
The source uses
\begin{equation}
 \mat H_m=-[\vct v]_\times,
 \qquad \mat R_m=r_m\mat I .
 \label{eq:widen-mag-effective-source}
\end{equation}
The deployed simulation/certificate configuration preserves this isotropy.  If
$\mat S_m=\mat H_m\mat P\mat H_m^\top+r_m\mat I$, then
\begin{equation}
 \mat H_m^\top\vct v=0,
 \qquad \mat S_m\vct v=r_m\vct v,
 \qquad \mat K_m\vct v=0 .
 \label{eq:widen-mag-radial-null}
\end{equation}
Thus the residual component parallel to $\vct v$ cannot change any estimator
state and cannot generate a quaternion injection or reset correction.  For the
exact rotational residual $\vct y_m=(\mat R(\vct c)-\mat I)\vct v$, define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct d_m:=\frac{\mat H_m^\top\vct y_m}{\|\vct v\|^2},
 \qquad
 \mat K_m\vct y_m=\mat K_m\mat H_m\vct d_m .}
 \label{eq:widen-mag-effective-coordinate}
\end{equation}
Writing $q=\|\vct c\|$, $\widehat{\vct v}=\vct v/\|\vct v\|$,
$\vct c_\perp=(\mat I-\widehat{\vct v}\widehat{\vct v}^\top)\vct c$, and
$\alpha=\vct c^\top\widehat{\vct v}$, the exact Cayley formula gives
\begin{equation}
 \vct d_m=
 \frac{4}{4+q^2}\vct c_\perp
 -\frac{2\alpha}{4+q^2}
   (\vct c_\perp\times\widehat{\vct v}).
 \label{eq:widen-mag-effective-formula}
\end{equation}
Consequently
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\vct d_m\|\le
 \frac{2}{\sqrt{4+q^2}}\|\vct c_\perp\|
 \le\|\vct c_\perp\|,
 \qquad
 \|\vct d_m-\vct c_\perp\|\le
 \frac{q}{\sqrt{4+q^2}}\|\vct c_\perp\|.}
 \label{eq:widen-mag-effective-bounds}
\end{equation}
The useful nonlinear magnetic residual is therefore an exact, nonexpansive
effective tangent coordinate rather than an adverse independent $\eta_m$ term.

The normal-Live accelerometer has an even stronger range property.  With the
configured optional lever arm disabled, its source Jacobian contains
\begin{equation}
 \mat J_{a_w}=\mat R_{wb},
 \qquad \mat J_{a_w}^\top\mat J_{a_w}=\mat I .
 \label{eq:widen-acc-effective-source}
\end{equation}
For a signed residual decomposition
$\vct y_a=\mat H_a\vct z+\vct\eta_a$, set
\begin{equation}
 \vct e_{\eta}:=\mat J_{a_w}^\top\vct\eta_a
 \label{eq:widen-acc-effective-aw}
\end{equation}
and let $\mat E_{a_w}$ inject this vector only into the $a_w$ coordinates.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mat H_a\mat E_{a_w}\vct e_\eta=\vct\eta_a,
 \qquad
 \mat K_a(\mat H_a\vct z+\vct\eta_a)
 =\mat K_a\mat H_a(\vct z+\mat E_{a_w}\vct e_\eta),
 \qquad
 \|\vct e_\eta\|=\|\vct\eta_a\|.}
 \label{eq:widen-acc-effective-identity}
\end{equation}
This is an exact reparameterization of the same implemented correction, not the
claim $\vct\eta_a=0$.  The Joseph information identity remains valid.  The
finite-angle Cayley geometry supplies the cellwise enclosure
\begin{equation}
 \|\vct e_\eta\|
 \le\frac{q^2}{\sqrt{4+q^2}}\,\bar f
 +\frac{2q}{\sqrt{4+q^2}}\,\|\delta\vct a_w\|,
 \label{eq:widen-acc-effective-bound}
\end{equation}
for the rotational remainder and rotated latent-acceleration cross term.
Additive bias/body terms remain in the linear source map.

Equations~\eqref{eq:widen-mag-effective-coordinate} and
\eqref{eq:widen-acc-effective-identity} retire the standalone vector-$\eta$
penalty from the active P5 numerical route.  The outward backend instead carries
$\mat P,\mat H,\mat R,\mat K,\vct r$ and the corresponding effective input in
one jointly source-reachable cell through the immediate quaternion injection and
left-error reset.  The same accelerometer reduction descends to the detectable
gravity quotient; it does not assign strict contraction to the neutral
$ b_{g,\parallel}$ coordinate.

The condition remains source faithful: it keeps the full $S\to\theta$ path,
does not assume scalar Wahba gains, and does not resurrect a Euclidean-radius
certificate.  The first-$S$ finite Cayley prefix and the exact transport algebra
are already certified.  The remaining P5 numerical task is therefore the
outward source-correlated propagation of the later one-second prediction,
vector, and $S$ prefixes, using the effective-input identities above and the
signed Cayley reset denominator.  The chart excludes the antipodal set and all
quantitative claims remain regional; no global MEKF claim is made.